  "behavior": [
    "All unadorned SQL ADD declarations use original14 directly, including Currency. Native/Access13 APIs and their exact decode/recovery language remain separate; no failed-proof retry or fake gallery policy is used.",
    "SqlUnadorned captured facts preserve native Text UTF-16 width and Decimal precision/scale. UI type/size summaries come from the private native plan; matching inert facts cannot replace the capability.",
    "Twelve distinct connected type journeys exercise actual SQL ADD, historical values, typed parameter UPDATE, NULL or Boolean-false clearing, then actual insertion/save/acknowledgement/reopen with complete independent images.",
    "Boolean omission remains explicitly refused without inventing a stored default; explicit Boolean input works. Text keeps nonempty Unicode/NULL distinct from empty strings and reaches fresh omitted NULL after the empty-string refusal.",
    "A generated/indexed journey deletes the largest live ID before ADD, preserves historical LAST and all index bytes, updates exact Currency 5.25, then inserts with next ID=LAST+1 and new Currency NULL.",
    "Exact14 routing covers stage, complete fresh requalification and both active/settled V3 recovery. Recovered committed operations report ColumnAdded without fabricated affected-row counts.",
    "The shared empty-Text declaration guard now applies to retained UPDATE17 producer and fresh proof before noop elimination, as well as INSERT. Absent AZL refuses; explicit true supports empty Text; explicit false retains normal field-constraint validation.",
    "Desktop stays a thin consuming host. MCP gallery editing rejects SQL origins and does not acquire an invented schema-SQL endpoint. The now-unused direct Desktop schema dependency is removed."
  ],
